.TH LOG-SUMMARY 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
log-summary \- count log lines by apparent severity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B log-summary
.RB [ --match " LITERAL]"
.RI [ LOGFILE | - ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a text log file or standard input (default). Counts lines
bearing common severity tokens (CRITICAL, ERROR, WARNING, NOTICE,
INFO, DEBUG, TRACE) or OTHER. Does not print log message contents.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --match " LITERAL"
Keep lines containing LITERAL, ignoring case. Not a regular expression.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B log-summary /var/log/syslog
.br
.B journalctl --no-pager -n 1000 | log-summary -
.SH NOTES
Keyword-based heuristic, not a syslog or structured log parser.
If multiple severity words occur, higher severity wins.
The program reads to EOF; it does not follow a growing file.
